# More tales (Living Server 1.2, owner 2026-11-18 09:14: "Yes to all the new tales"): the seventeen open-world raids (the
# five Wretches of Winter share one tale), Myrddraxis, Behemoth, and fireside versions for the thin places of the lore
# audit (LORE-028). Same rules as tales.lines: topic "tale_<lore id>" or "fireside_<lore id>"; role B is the storyteller
# ({name_b}); A asks, C hushes, D begs and asks, E has heard it too often, F is new. A fireside's id may be a place's lore
# file when the place has no boss file (Keltoi Fogou, Cursed Tomb, Nisse's Lair, Vendo Caverns, Koalinth Caverns).
#
# Every mechanic told here is one the server's fight has (data/lore/bosses/<id>.json facts, the boss scripts). Named heroes,
# sayings and customs are the lore bible's own writing and are told as stories ("the woodsmen say"), never as canon.
# A teller types: short sentences, one idea a line. No tale here ends by repeating the teller's last phrase.

@kind debate
@realm alb

@topic tale_green-knight
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_green-knight
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b} you about? tell the green knight one | {name_b}, the knight up in sauvage. whats his story
C: shh all, {name_b} is doing sauvage | quiet in faction a sec, green knight story
?E: the one where nobody whispers to him. i know it | here we go, defend it defend it
D: please {name_b}, i ride past him every day and never knew | go on, i only know hes green and big
B: alright alright. find a stump and sit
B: north edge of forest sauvage, where the road climbs to the pennines. thats where he stands
B: the woodsmen say he was there before the castle. the bards say before arthur
B: he greets everyone who stops. warns them the forest turns on those who wake it
B: and then he waits. he has never drawn on anyone who did not ask
?F: ask how? | so you have to start it?
B: you whisper to him. defend it. old hopcyn cut wood there forty years and saw three men ask
~ 8
D: and what happens when you ask? | ok so someone asks. then what?
B: the deadwood stands up. a rotten felwood tears out of the ground at every mans feet
B: so forty of you fight forty trees as well as him
B: his sword sets the air on fire round whoever it hits. stand at that mans shoulder and you burn too
B: and he knows who keeps a company standing. now and then he walks past the tanks to cut at a healer
?E: guard your clerics. every time | yeah he loves a cleric
B: hurt him and he breaks off. walks to another clearing, never the same one twice running
B: takes a breath there and heals a little. only a little. follow him and keep cutting
B: leave him alone a minute though and hes whole. bows to the empty road and the trees lie down
~ 25
F: wait so who whispers? not me | i am never stopping on that road again
C: and the bards still think hes owed a blow from the old gawain story | ok but who here has actually been thrown in with forty trees

@topic tale_coliath
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_coliath
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b} whats coliath actually guarding on gwyddneau? you know it | {name_b}, tell the lich on the height
C: oh this is a good one. hush | everyone quiet, coliath story
D: yes please, i only ever saw it from the lammia town | tell it {name_b}, nobody i ask agrees
B: ok. sit. this one has three endings
B: coliath stands on the highest ground of gwyddneau. above the north end of the lammia town
B: its one of morgana's liches. a dead mage she kept past its death
B: it has never left that height. not to chase, not to feed. not once since the first year of her war
?F: so whats up there? | guarding what though?
B: thats the oldest wager in the isle of glass garrison. the garrison says treasure. soldiers always do
B: the lammia of clifton say a drowned country's king is buried under it
B: and the lacula sept say it guards nothing but itself. a lich keeps its death close
~ 8
D: and the dead round it? where did they come from | does it stand alone up there?
B: no. when it came, the ancient dead climbed out of the drowned ground. they stood round it
B: they turn with it when anyone comes up the slope. break them and the height stays bare till it comes back
B: and when it dies they all drop with it
?E: and the end is the bad part | wait for the drinking. thats where we wiped
B: the lacula have a saying. a lich near its end stops striking and starts drinking
B: low on life it drops its arms. then it drains whoever is in front of it. follows them anywhere
B: everything it drinks it keeps. the lammia say be quicker than its thirst
~ 25
F: so which one is it, the king or the lich itself? | nobody ever settled it?
C: the lacula bury their dead facing the height. to watch if anyone ever is quicker | i still say treasure

@topic tale_spirit-of-lord-emthoro
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_spirit-of-lord-emthoro
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b}, the ghost lord on inishail. tell it | {name_b} tell us about emthoro, the one the orcs serve
C: hush for {name_b}, inishail story | quiet all. emthoro
D: please, i got "immune to your damage" on him and gave up | go on {name_b}, i want to know why nothing hits him
B: right. ears open
B: lord emthoro held inishail before the war. the colleges lost his name, or never wrote it down
B: he held the isle the old way. by standing on it
B: he walked his bounds. heard his tenants at his own door
B: and no order counted unless the sender stood on his ground first
?F: even the colleges? | so messengers had to walk up to him?
B: the college of the old tongues sent messengers twice. both walked up from the shore. they wrote it down, annoyed
~ 8
D: so did morgana raise him? | how did he end up dead there?
B: no. the war reached the isle and he was standing before his door. he is standing there now
B: the readers at caer gothwaite think her war did not make him. the only one
B: and his old way still holds. from beyond his ground nothing reaches him. arrows, spells, stones
B: you have to come up and stand there. and then something goes out of all of you. into him
?E: and the more of you up there the more he drinks | pack in close and he heals off the lot of you
B: he wont step off to follow anyone. a lord does not chase his tenants. they come to him
B: and they do. the dead of the isle and the orcs who fled krondon. his tenants now, unasked
~ 25
F: so the orcs work for a ghost and never signed anything | i would read stolen books too
D: the lammia say you go up and stay till he leaves. thats the only way out of a tenancy | ok, everyone stands on his ground. got it

@realm mid

@topic tale_glacier-giant
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_glacier-giant
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b}, tell the young ones about the giant at odins gate | {name_b} you on? the glacier giant one, come on
C: quiet in the hall. {name_b} has the giant | shh, odins gate story
?E: ah, the flying lessons | this is the one where we all land in a snowbank
D: tell it {name_b}. i have only seen him from the keep wall | please, the whole thing this time
B: ha. sit, sit. mind the snow on your boots
B: odins gate has a giant and a glacier. and no gate
B: hes stood there longer than the frontier keeps. a hill of blue ice with a face
B: he does not walk like other giants. he stands. the skalds argue what for
?F: what do they think? | guarding something?
B: some say a door the gods left at the foot of asgard's road. folded into the ice like a letter
B: some say hes just a giant who found a good spot
~ 8
D: and the throwing? | what is the throwing about?
B: once you fight him he picks one of you up and throws. not across a room. across the land
B: the warders of the frontier keep a book of where everyone lands
B: and he does not throw the one in front of him. he reaches past for someone further back
B: like a doorman reaching past a beggar for the one slipping in behind
?E: so the tank is the only safe one there | yeah stand at the back and see what happens
B: near the end he stops throwing. just stands and takes it. like the door was not worth keeping
B: and leave him be a little while and he is whole again
~ 25
F: hang on. what happens if the gate ever opens? | so is there a door or not
A: nobody alive knows. good one {name_b} | thanks {name_b}. i am standing in front from now on

@topic tale_mortufoghus
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_mortufoghus
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b} tell the mortufoghus one. the mammoth on modernagrav | {name_b}, the big cow by the bones. story please
C: ale down, {name_b} is telling the mammoth | hush. modernagrav
?E: the cow. we are really doing the cow | moo
D: go on, i want to know why the morvalt love her | tell it {name_b}, i only know she throws people
B: good. a cold one for a cold night
B: the morvalt say she was there when they came through the wall
B: the dwarves at the post saw them come. first thing beyond the gap was a mammoth taller than a longhouse
B: walking a path she had already worn knee deep round the bones
?F: what bones? | the skeleton they dig at?
B: the huge one half buried in the island. the morvalt came across looking for the mother
B: the morvalt think shes the mother's guardian. or the mother's own spirit walking. they argue at their fires
B: our scholars note the oldest tale starts with a cow in the ice. licking the first things out of the rime
~ 8
D: so how does she fight? | what does she do to you?
B: the one in front she tramples. her tusks leave you dazed, cant lift a hand
B: the cold rolls off her in one breath. over everyone crowded near her target
B: and the ones hanging back at the edge, she reaches past and flings. high and far
?E: and the fall hurts. ask me how i know | flung past two spoil heaps once. walked back
B: orri of hagall saw her throw a digger. the digger got up and went back to his spade
B: he wrote that the morvalt seemed to think it an honour
~ 25
F: so do you want to be thrown or not? | an honour. sure. i will take the trampling
C: i still think they are digging up a cow | the morvalt stand in front of her on purpose. braver than me

@topic tale_raumarik-revenant
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_raumarik-revenant
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b}, the revenant in raumarik. tell the young ones | {name_b} tell the one about the sun splinter
C: hush in faction, {name_b} has the revenant | quiet, raumarik story
D: please, i did fenrir's folly and never got the why | yes go on {name_b}, who was he
B: very well. ale first, then the cold
B: nobody remembers who he was. the galplen tellers start with a blizzard
B: fenrir spat a splinter of the sun into the snow. and one of the dead felt it from across a valley
B: he crawled to it on his hands. he thought it was a hearth
B: he lay down beside it. warm for the first time since he died
?F: and then? | thats almost nice
B: and he decided nobody else would ever be warm like that
~ 8
D: so he built the fortress? | where does he keep it?
B: on the north west heights. stone by stone with dead hands that never tired
B: the wraiths and wights on the slopes want what he has. he lets none of them in
B: he keeps no guard either. trusts nobody to stand on his walls
B: every intruder in his hall gets the cold of the land. a frost shock with nearly every blow
?E: and your spells barely tickle him | yeah casters, bring a sword
B: spells slide off him more than steel. the tellers say he sat so long by the sun. our magic feels like a little warmth
B: steel is cold. he understands cold. so steel reaches him
B: no rope holds him either, and no sleep charm finds anything to sleep
~ 25
F: so the splinter just goes back to him? every time? | gris makes the caskets and it glows through anyway?
A: always does, the tellers say. thanks {name_b} | that one always makes me want a fire

@topic tale_wretch-of-winter
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_wretch-of-winter
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b}, the wretch of winter. all of it, the shells and the jarl's son | {name_b} tell the wretch one, theres new ppl
C: shh all. the wretch | quiet in the hall, raumarik story
?E: the scary one for the new folk. sure | this is how they got me as a young one
D: go on {name_b}. i thought it was five different things | please, i want to know what it actually is
B: fine. horns full? then listen
B: winter in raumarik has a wretch. and the wretch has no shape of its own
B: it borrows. where a scorpion died in the snow it gets up in the scorpion's shell
B: spider, crab, jotun, arachite. nine shapes counted around raumarik. one hunger in different coats
?F: what is it underneath? | so whats wearing the coats?
B: the galplen tellers say the cold itself, tired of waiting for things to die
B: the fenrir mystics say its the wolf's breath of the last winter. sent ahead
B: the skalds of jordheim say it was a jarl's son. he ran from a battle in the snow
~ 8
D: why did odin's maidens not take him? | what happened to the boy?
B: he froze while hiding. odin's maidens refused him. the cursed tomb refused him too
B: he had not even died properly. so the cold took him in
B: and he tries on other people's deaths, looking for one that fits
B: in a beast's shell it bites like the beast. leaves poison working in you
B: in a giant or a dead man it uses the cold. a frost shock from the hand
?E: and no root or mez touches it | dont bother with the mezzer
B: break the shape and the wretch is not broken. somewhere else in raumarik the snow stands up
~ 25
F: ...so killing one does nothing? | nine of them. great
C: so which coat is it wearing tonight | anyone else checking the snow behind them now

@realm hib

@topic tale_evern
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_evern
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b}, tell evern. the stones in breifine | {name_b} the fairy lord one, please, for the new folk
C: gather in, {name_b} is telling evern | hush, breifine
D: go on. i walk past his ring on every keep run | yes {name_b}, all of it
B: very well. come in near the stones
B: evern was standing in breifine when the frontier was only hills
B: the keeps were built round his ring of stones because nobody could move them. or him
B: the sylvan think he is a great lord of the fairy kind. gone strange with age
?F: then why is he still here? | did he choose to stay?
B: the druids think his ring was a gate once. he stayed to keep it after it closed
B: the little wraith fairies of the frontier are his last subjects
~ 8
D: and the fairies, what do they do in a fight? | how do the fairies help him?
B: when he is hurt they drift in on the wind. two, three, five of them
B: they gather by his stones and pour healing into him. a great deal at a time
B: so the fairies die first. always the fairies
?E: and dont drag him off the ring | pull him off his stones and nothing lands
B: away from his ring he cannot be hurt at all. hits just slide off
B: and let him alone a little while. he is whole and the fairies are gone
B: under breifine run the marfach caves and the road to the summoners
~ 25
F: so is he sitting on something? | hold on, whats under breifine then
C: the old frontier hands think so. nobody has lifted him off it to check | kill the fairies first. i am writing that down

@topic tale_juggernaut
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_juggernaut
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b}, what is the juggernaut? the thing in the cursed forest | {name_b} tell the juggernaut story
C: quiet, {name_b} is telling the cursed forest one | everyone hush a moment
D: please. even the trees move for him | go on {name_b}, i never knew what he was
B: yes, if you let me finish this time
B: nobody knows what he was before he walked the cursed forest
B: he has no court. no servants. no tricks
B: he walks his long road through the rotten wood. walking trees, blights and dark men all get out of his way
?F: why do they move? | even the unseelie?
B: the seelie and the unseelie quarrel about everything. they agree on one thing. give him the road
B: the sylvan think he is the broken bargain itself. given a body so neither court has to hold it
~ 8
D: so how do you fight a bargain? | what is the trick to him then?
B: there is none. he just hits harder than anything his size should
B: and he follows you a long way down his road. then he turns for home
?E: run and he keeps coming. trust me | i tried kiting him once. once
B: warriors swear the colours lie about him. the scholars say the colours are right and the warriors are scared
B: both may be true
B: when he falls the whole forest holds its breath. to see if the debt is paid
~ 25
F: and is it? | so is it ever paid
A: never is. he comes back. thank you {name_b} | he always comes back. lovely telling, {name_b}

@topic tale_curengkur
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_curengkur
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b}, the thing the mantids whisper about in allta fearann. tell it | {name_b} tell curengkur. the nest one
C: softly now. {name_b} has the wild land story | hush, allta fearann
D: please, i want to know why the bugs go quiet | go on {name_b}, all of it
B: come closer then. this one is told low
B: allta fearann is the wild land. high country north of vigilant rock
B: the mantids held it before the sylvan named it. a hard busy people. not friends, not enemies
B: they are not afraid of much. they are afraid of curengkur
?F: what is it? | why are they scared?
B: it hunts them where they nest. and it has a nest of its own
B: a hollow on the high ground. the air above it burns
~ 8
D: what is in the nest? | so what does the nest do?
B: when curengkur is roused the nest wakes with it. the air round it sears whoever stands there. over and over
B: and curengkur spits acid. it hangs round its prey and eats through shell and skin
B: it strikes from further off than any mantid can reach too
?E: and it heals on the nest. fast | fight it at home and you lose
B: the mantids' oldest warning. curengkur is never wounded at home. a hurt that would kill it closes on the nest
B: so their old hunters go up, sting it and run. draw it down the slope till the air is cool. then turn
B: most of them die doing it. the mantids say its still better than the nest
~ 25
F: so we pull it off the nest. got it | drag it away then fight. ok
C: when it dies you can hear the mantids clicking all over the high country. for a while | if the mantids go quiet, turn round

@topic tale_marfoirwort
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_marfoirwort
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b}, the killer plant in cothrom gorge. tell it | {name_b} tell marfoirwort, the bare ring one
C: hush all, {name_b} has the gorge story | quiet, marfoirwort
D: please, i did writhing death and never learned about the big one | tell it {name_b}
B: softly then, this one is old
B: marfoirwort is the oldest thing growing in cothrom gorge. the gorge sylvan named it the killer plant
B: they were not being poetic
B: it stands at the west head of the gorge. in a wide ring of bare ground
B: nothing has grown in that ring for an age. everything that ever grew there, it drank
?F: what does it live on then? | no soil?
B: it lives on what walks near it
~ 8
D: so how does it kill? | what happens when it hits you?
B: it strikes one of you. and the life goes out of everyone standing close round that one
B: all that strength goes into marfoirwort. closes its own wounds
B: so the oldest custom of the gorge. a sylvan crossing near the ring crosses alone
B: one throat is a meal. five throats together feed it for a season
?E: and every captain still stands too close | spread out. please. spread out
B: third summer of the isles, swords from tir na nog came to burn it
B: they stood shoulder to shoulder round it. the way a good company stands round anything
B: it drank from all of them every strike. whole by evening. the captain planted a rowan for the dead
~ 25
F: shoulder to shoulder. ouch | so the trick is just dont stand together?
C: and the gorge folk watch the ring for the day it starts to widen | cronwort on the east floor worries me now

@topic tale_mollunero
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_mollunero
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b}, the cold mother at worlds end. tell it | {name_b} tell mollunero, the pool one
C: hush, worlds end story | everyone quiet, {name_b} has the octonoid
D: please, the fishers wont say her name | go on {name_b}, i want the grandmothers version too
B: yes. i will name her, though the fishers wont
B: mollunero. strongest of the three mothers on the world's end shore
B: she lies in the deep pool below the cliffs on the south shore
B: the sea comes in through a gap there and stays cold in high summer. the fishers say the cold is hers
?F: so its her making it cold? | how cold?
B: fishing lines that touch her come up stiff with frost
~ 8
D: and the grandmothers story? | what do the grandmothers say?
B: that she lets her brood fight for her. she comes out when every child is dead
B: coll of the domnann guides has seen her come up. he says thats a story for grandchildren
B: she comes up with her young. seven or eight of them, near as heavy as a man
B: the story has one true thing in it. the children never outlive her. she sinks, they sink
?E: and whoever she holds goes grey | the cold blast on the tank. ugh
B: her arms are the worst. the cold of the pool goes into whoever she holds, again and again
B: the fishers say warm him faster than she cools him. and no charm holds her
~ 25
F: so heal the tank and ignore the grandmothers. ok | warm him faster. thats the whole fight
C: the fomorians left her twice the catch they left balere, flann of howth wrote | i will never fish that shore again

# Myrddraxis, under Fomor. Fomor has no raid in this world (its navmesh has no path to the chamber): his tale is told on
# its own, and the rumour after it is lore, never a raid.

@topic tale_myrddraxis
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_myrddraxis
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b}, the hydra under fomor. tell the whole thing | {name_b} tell myrddraxis. the egg one
C: gather round, {name_b} has the hydra | hush, fomor story
?E: five heads and all of them hungry. i know | here comes the egg
D: please {name_b}, i heard the heads heal each other | go on, what is it really
B: well then. it was an egg once
B: grey green and warm. a hydrar found it digging the lowest cistern of fomor, in the black sand
B: the fomorians call it a gift of the sea. the sylvan call it a theft from the deep places
B: the druids of tir na nog say an ollpheist. a great water worm, like the lough derg tales
?F: how did it get five heads? | was it always that big?
B: it hatched with one head and grew five. one hunger with five mouths
B: whatever any mouth tears from you mends the great body. and the other mouths a little
B: it never leaves its mound. step out of its reach and it burns you where you stand
~ 8
D: so how did anyone ever kill it? | what does it do when you hurt it?
B: hurt it deep and it bellows. the whole cistern stands still and stares
B: before the great breath it draws in till the water sinks. then fire across everything
B: the hydrars sing it. the beast draws in, the wise go out
B: and between breaths one head looks at one of you. gathering fire slow enough to see
?E: so walk away from your friends | the one it looks at walks off. always
B: rionach of tir na nog's company cut the mouths one at a time. when the small heads hung in the water the body could not mend
B: the earth lurched. a light on the mound, like where a dragon falls
~ 25
F: so it counts as a dragon? | a dragon with no wings. huh
C: when balor's eye opens all the way, the hydrars will let it swim east | a scale is a closed door. bring a key, not a song

# Behemoth, on the ledge above Legion: no raid of its own (the Darkness Falls raid's tale stays Legion's). Every realm
# tells it.

@realm *

@topic tale_behemoth
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_behemoth
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b}, the thing on the ledge in df. what is it actually | {name_b} tell behemoth, the new folk keep pulling it
C: shh. {name_b} is telling the ledge | quiet for this one, all of you
D: please. i have only ever seen it breathing up there | go on {name_b}, why does nobody fight it
B: alright. this ones short, because it does not do much
B: every account of the hollow agrees. the behemoth was there first. before the lords
B: the inquisitors say the hollow is just the shape it left lying down
B: it is not a demon. it does not speak or bargain or eat souls. its on no roll
?F: so what is it then? | not a demon??
B: the church reads it out of job. the beast of the first making. the skalds call it one of the old ones
B: the druids say its a hill that has not decided to lie still yet
~ 8
D: and legion? why does he leave it alone? | what happened at the feast?
B: at the feast of thrones it lay along the wall. it did not fight or kneel
B: when the master had eaten nineteen lords he looked at it. it looked back. he did not try
B: the imps say he was afraid. the inquisitors say it has no place in the bargain
?E: and it kills anything it touches. anything | it does not miss. it does not need to
B: whatever it swings at, it ends. shield, mail, quick feet. landed or not
B: its slow to notice anyone not close to its nose. its hide turns blades and drinks spells
B: an albion knight who had killed legion once took eighty onto the ledge. it lifted its head and he was gone
~ 25
F: so we just leave it alone? | then what is it even for?
C: brother odran's door book says do not count it. count your own and go home | the imps still take any bet against it

# Campfire versions of the tales above: told in /group by a groupmate while the party rests in or near the place.

@realm alb

@topic fireside_green-knight
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_green-knight
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: anyone know the rule with the green knight? the woodsmen have one | you know the knight up the road only fights if you ask
?B: ask how | what rule
A: you whisper defend it. thats the asking. he warns everyone and waits
A: old hopcyn cut wood here forty years and saw three men ask
A: and when one does, a dead tree stands up at every mans feet
B: so nobody whisper anything. good | noted. i am not whispering to anybody
A: {name_b} tells the long one in faction. the clearings bit is good

@topic fireside_coliath
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_coliath
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: see that height to the north? coliath has stood there since the war started | ever wonder what the lich up there guards
?B: treasure? | no idea
A: the garrison says treasure. the clifton lammia say a drowned king under it
A: the lacula sept reckon its own death is the treasure. liches hide those close
A: and it never comes down. not once. so we are fine sitting here
B: unless someone pulls it | i am holding you to that
A: {name_b} knows the whole story, if you ask nice in faction

@topic fireside_spirit-of-lord-emthoro
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_spirit-of-lord-emthoro
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: the orcs here serve a ghost, you know. emthoro | funny thing about the orc village here
A: he held this isle by standing on it. still does
A: nothing hits him from off his ground. you have to go up and stand there
?B: and then? | that sounds bad
A: then he drinks from everyone stood up there. more of you, more he drinks
B: right. so we skip him tonight | the orcs can keep him
A: ask {name_b} sometime, they know the messengers part

@realm mid

@topic fireside_glacier-giant
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_glacier-giant
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: the warders keep a book of where the giant throws people. a whole book | ever see the glacier giant throw someone
?B: a book? | how far
A: across the land. high. he never throws the one in front, he reaches past
A: the skalds think hes guarding a door folded up in the ice
A: and the grandmothers of jamtland say he kneels the night it opens
B: lot of standing around for a door | i would pay to see that
A: get {name_b} to tell it in faction. they do it properly

@topic fireside_mortufoghus
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_mortufoghus
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: the mammoth was here before the morvalt came through the wall | know why the morvalt dont fight mortufoghus
?B: why not | because shes huge?
A: they think shes the mother's guardian. or the mother herself walking
A: she wears a path round the bones older than the dig
A: and getting flung by her counts as an honour to them
B: i will pass on the honour | they can have it
A: {name_b} tells it better, with the digger and the spade

@topic fireside_raumarik-revenant
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_raumarik-revenant
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: the revenant up north sits on a piece of the sun | you know what the revenant keeps in that fort
?B: a piece of what | the sun?
A: a splinter fenrir spat into the snow. he crawled to it in a blizzard
A: he was warm for the first time since he died. so nobody else gets to be
A: take it off him and it creeps back to him across the snow
B: well i am cold, so i get it | sounds like my uncle
A: {name_b} does the full saga in faction now and then

@topic fireside_wretch-of-winter
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_wretch-of-winter
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: they tell new groups about the wretch out here to scare them. want to hear it | the wretch of winter. you know it?
?B: go on | no?
A: it has no shape. it borrows dead things. a scorpion, a crab, a jotun
A: break one and the wretch walks off. somewhere else the snow gets up
A: the skalds say its a jarl's son who froze hiding from a fight
B: ...is that snow moving over there | ok that worked. i am scared
A: ask {name_b} for the long version, all nine coats

@realm hib

@topic fireside_evern
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_evern
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: those stones over there are evern's. the keeps were built round them | you know why nobody moved evern's stones
?B: too heavy? | why
A: nobody could. not the stones, not him. he was here before the frontier
A: the wraith fairies come in on the wind and heal him off the stones
A: the old hands think he sits on a lid. marfach is right under us
B: lets not lift it tonight | i will just sit very still then
A: {name_b} tells it in faction. kill the fairies first is the moral

@topic fireside_juggernaut
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_juggernaut
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: if the trees step off the road, the juggernaut is coming | you know why the walking trees here step aside sometimes
?B: why | what for
A: the juggernaut. both courts agree on one thing. give him the road
A: the sylvan say hes the broken bargain with a body
A: no tricks. he just hits too hard and chases too far
B: so we give him the road too | i am giving him the whole forest
A: {name_b} tells it better in faction, the colours bit

@topic fireside_curengkur
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_curengkur
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: notice how quiet the mantids are? thats a bad sign up here | if the mantids go quiet, we turn round. rule of the wild land
?B: why | whats that mean
A: curengkur is back. it hunts them where they nest
A: its own nest burns the air, and heals it while it stands there
A: their hunters sting it and run to drag it off. most dont make it
B: ok. i am listening for clicking now | nobody pull anything big
A: {name_b} has the whole story. ask in faction

@topic fireside_marfoirwort
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_marfoirwort
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: the bare ring at the head of the gorge. thats marfoirwort's | see the ground where nothing grows? old plant lives there
?B: a plant? | what about it
A: it drank everything that ever grew there. now it drinks whoever walks close
A: hit one of you and it drinks from everyone stood round. heals off all of it
A: so the sylvan here cross near it one at a time. oldest custom in the gorge
B: we are spread out from now on | one at a time. got it
A: {name_b} knows the captain who learned the hard way

@topic fireside_mollunero
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_mollunero
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: the pool down below the cliffs. dont touch the water | the fishers here never fish the south pool. know why
?B: why | cold?
A: mollunero. the strongest mother on this shore
A: lines that touch her come up frozen
A: she rises with her brood round her. when she sinks, they all sink
B: i am staying dry | not fishing tonight then
A: {name_b} tells it better. ask about the grandmothers story

@topic fireside_myrddraxis
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_myrddraxis
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: the hydra down in the cistern was an egg once. a hydrar dug it up | know what the hydrars sing about the thing below
?B: what | the hydra?
A: eat and be whole, eat and be many, eat and be ours
A: every bite it takes mends the body and the other heads
A: when one head looks at you, walk away from your friends. domnann rule
B: noted. very noted | i will walk far away, thanks
A: {name_b} has the full one in faction

@realm *

@topic fireside_behemoth
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_behemoth
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: the thing on the ledge was here before the demons | ever wonder about the behemoth up on its ledge
?B: not really | what about the thing
A: its no demon. it was in this hollow before the lords came
A: at the feast of thrones even legion looked at it and left it be
A: whatever it swings at dies. so dont go near its nose
B: not planning to | i give it a very wide berth
A: {name_b} tells it in faction. the knight and his eighty

# Fireside versions for the thin places (LORE-028): a short tale of one boss there, or of the place itself when it has no
# boss file. These have no faction tale; a groupmate tells them while the party rests there.

@realm alb

@topic fireside_overseer-tepok
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_overseer-tepok
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: tepok stood at this mine's door an hour once. before the goblins took it | you know the overseer here can write
?B: a goblin? writing? | write what
A: he kept the old reeve's tally after. copied the reeve's notes for a season till he got it
A: keeps his office by the mouth. cant count a door he cant see
A: captain rhodri read his sack. tepok writes letters, and they get answered
B: answered by who though | thats worse than if he just hit things
A: {name_b} might know more, ask in faction

@topic fireside_keltoi-fogou
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_keltoi-fogou
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: the keltoi didnt bury anyone in here. they put their young in | know what this place was for
?B: their young? | for what
A: shut them in at dusk with whatever lives past fear. opened it the third day
A: they kept a count on the wall. who went in, who came out
A: the two counts dont agree. the dalesmen say fane is the difference
B: and fane is still down here | lovely. lets go deeper then
A: the keltoi never came up when rome came. or when rome left

@topic fireside_lich-lord-ilron
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_lich-lord-ilron
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: the priests in ilron's gallery are all him. younger him | ever hear how you find the real ilron
?B: how | which one is real?
A: only one of them ever aged. the old one, heavier in the hand
A: stand close to the young ones and you fall asleep
A: they vanish when he falls. hit them and you waste it on shadows
B: find the oldest. ok | so look for grandpa
A: a squire from the black mountains spotted him first. ask {name_b} for that one

@topic fireside_scurceol-hyrde
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_scurceol-hyrde
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: the storm keeper in krondon was chosen in an open boat in a gale | know how krondon picked its storm keepers
?B: a boat? | how
A: took the boys out in a storm. the one who stood and wasnt thrown out got the job
A: he has four airs bound up in the corners. while they shine nothing bites him
A: hit an air and sometimes it drops you across the room
B: bows on the corners then | so the lights go first
A: {name_b} knows the sea captain who did it first

@topic fireside_lady-darra
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_lady-darra
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: lady darra was a nurse here. a miller's girl from the severn | you know who the lady upstairs was
?B: who | a knight?
A: a nurse. ran the watch sickroom twenty years, married lord gildas
A: her four knights stand the corners and heal her now
A: drop all four first or she never tires
B: that is sad and annoying | corners first. sure
A: {name_b} knows her letters to the prioress, ask them

@realm mid

@topic fireside_jarl-ormarr
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_jarl-ormarr
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: the jarl down the east galleries took this mine for iron | you know the two sayings about jarl ormarr
?B: no | what sayings
A: no song holds the jarl. a spaewife sang his hall asleep once. he sat awake
A: and strike the jarl, wake the hall. hit him and his huscarls come
A: he went down after his son's shift and never came back up
B: so no mez, and his friends come. great | he sounds like my old guild leader
A: {name_b} tells the whole saga, with aros and all

@topic fireside_aros-the-spiritmaster
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_aros-the-spiritmaster_2
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: you hear the voices down here sometimes. thats aros's mine | the skalds say aros still reads out names down here
?B: names? | whose names
A: the shift that broke into the cold seam. he promised none would be forgotten
A: the mistress of runes cut not here. nobody listened
A: the jarl went down after his son, forty huscarls with him
B: and here we are, past the seam | i didnt hear any names. i didnt
A: ask {name_b} for the aros one in faction. its long

@topic fireside_cursed-tomb
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_cursed-tomb
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: this tomb is for the ones odin's maidens passed by | ever wonder who ends up in here
?B: who | bad people?
A: runners, oathbreakers. men who sold their friends. dishonoured dead
A: they bring them in at night, no torches, so the gods wont look
A: the draugr still drill down here. like one more drill could undo the running
B: we are not running then | nobody run. ever
A: the way keeper counts who passes. so be counted

@topic fireside_nisses-lair
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_nisses-lair
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: every farm had a tomte once. you gave him butter in his porridge at midwinter | know why the tomte live down here
?B: and if you forgot? | porridge?
A: forget the butter and he goes bad. these are the ones who got forgotten too often
A: nisse was the tomte of the first farm in svealand
A: he still remembers the name of the family that forgot him
B: i always put butter in. always | someone tell my mother
A: they keep prisoners down here too. from farms that skimped

@topic fireside_vendo-caverns
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_vendo-caverns
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: every young warrior of mularn gets walked up here. trainers' custom | you know the vendo were here before mularn was a village
?B: and they never stopped fighting? | before mularn?
A: two peoples fighting over one hillside forever. neither wins, neither stops
A: the trainers would be sorry if it ended. best teacher in the vale
A: the svendo down deep howl the hours. sometimes it all stops at once
B: and then? | i hope it doesnt stop tonight
A: dont whistle down here either. grjotgard answers

@topic fireside_hresvelgr
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_hresvelgr
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: the werewolf king in here has three names. you greet all three | know why there are three kings in the regal chamber
?B: three? | why three
A: hresvelgr, king hresvelgr, hresveigr. wolf, man, and the thing between
A: they stand side by side. nobody in the haven speaks to only one
A: the gothi send us to kill him. the wolfaur say we only ever kill the man
B: so the wolf just walks off after | that explains the respawn
A: he is the one who sent the dragon's envoy home. wolves answer to the pack

@realm hib

@topic fireside_king-vian
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_king-vian
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: king vian down south listens more than he talks. in a bear thats unsettling | ever met the ursine king in here
?B: no | is he nasty?
A: not cruel looking. sits with his old and young, listens
A: his line won the old quarrel and put the losers in collars
A: but the forge below never bowed to him. the dreaded ursine keeps it
B: a king who cant reach his own fire. huh | so hes waiting for it to go out
A: hervelina says that is exactly why he listens

@topic fireside_koalinth-caverns
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_koalinth-caverns
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: the koalinth came up out of the sea one spring. nobody knows why | ever wonder why fish people live in a cave
?B: why | they got lost?
A: tir urphost dates it to the spring the mist lifted off hy brasil
A: they hold fights in the big cave. spectators and all, like the old kings
A: and they keep a door open to the sea. their envoys go down and come back
B: talking to who | i dont want to know what is down there
A: the druids whisper that something drove them up. or sent them

@topic fireside_eraliwyr
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_eraliwyr
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: the alchemist at the north crossing is polite. right up until hes not | you know eraliwyr, by spriggit?
?B: the potion guy? | who
A: he works down here where nobody watches him
A: a druid woman took a cough cup from him once. ended up a skeleton on the wind
A: he talks about the weather and the price of jade. then he attacks
B: so dont buy anything from him | i will skip the small talk
A: the druids still keep the jade jar from that

@topic fireside_ancient-black-oak
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_ancient-black-oak
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: the black oak grows out of caimheul's grave. she planted it | know where the big black oak came from
?B: who planted it | from where
A: the eldest keener. an acorn from the bog of the oak, first night of the keen
A: it doesnt want anything from you if you dont want anything from it
A: hit it and roots come up in a ring and hold your feet
B: so leave the tree alone | i want nothing from it. nothing
A: when the lady falls its just a dead tree till her keen comes back

@topic fireside_black-lady
@levels 1-50
@scene fireside_black-lady_2
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
A: the black lady was caimheul's foster mother. they hired her to keen him anyway | ever hear who the black lady was
?B: keen? | who
A: a keener sings facing the road. never looks back at the grave
A: on the fourth night something below spoke to her. and she looked back
A: next morning the chieftain was standing
B: so its all one sad family down here | nobody tell me the rest tonight
A: the hill keeners say end the singer and the grief goes with her
